unded tree work, no old payload/manifest scan, and the final other-repository conflict with all pass values unchanged. Preserve original debits, caps, deadlines, authority and payload admission. This finding concerns required acceptance evidence.\n\nArchitecture: the shared ledger, finish reservation, closed Native frames before parent awaits, fresh metadata comparisons and one-use preparation form a coherent boundary. No additional architectural finding identified.\n\nSecurity: exact native pin/data/place admission, whole-prefix privacy checks, narrow public Membership-copy handling and bounded reader/append validation are preserved in the reviewed code. Caller anchors, values observed at those anchors and omission byte counts remain explicit trust. Omitted text is not proof of its digest, body or field bound. TEST provider/policy/authority evidence does not establish hosted or deployment admission.\n\nSimplification: the scalar metadata plans and shared pure cost formulas keep forecasting separate from payload access; literal prior-cost receipts provide useful independent checks. Complete the existing witness without adding another archive abstraction.\n\nValidation: verified the closed grant and 2,872 explicit copied leaves; independently matched all 2,703 captured source paths, bytes and executable modes to the candidate Git tree. Parsed 2,075 unique terminal cases: 2,072 passed and three skipped, zero unhandled errors. Raw logs also show repository Node 33/33 and Counting Node 55/55. Original natural gate exit 0; outer 804.78 seconds and 1,093.50 CPU seconds on the recorded shared host. Dependency inventory is producer evidence; I did not independently rehash the full dependency tree after the run. Checker diff --check passes; no runtime test or whole gate rerun. No deployment or landing approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2ad9744df9b28d1ccdb83ac7485994e1188f6be","binding":"assigned","head":"be0c40b5df29914